      "tail": "<scene-comp> defines 'onSceneAddition' — on<Event>-shaped member name(s), which collide with the elements factory's event-handler sugar. Since 1.8.0, IF the member holds a function when the creator runs, it wins: creator({ onSceneAddition: fn }) assigns it rather than attaching a 'sceneaddition' listener (tosijs#22) — and then that name can no longer carry event sugar. A member declared but left undefined/null still gets event sugar, so the meaning depends on initialisation: give it a function default, or rename to handle<Event> for a component callback / add<Event>Listener for something that registers a listener.\n\n 1118 pass\n 0 fail\n 3122 expect() calls\nRan 1118 tests across 38 files. [12.16s]"
    },
